---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Projects - Sally Kang">
	<article class="projects-page">
        <h2 class="page-title">Projects</h2>
        
        <div class="projects-content">
            <h3>AI & Agent</h3>
            
            <div class="project-item featured">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="https://github.com/SallyKAN/lumos">Lumos</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">Python</span>
                        <span class="tag">2026</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>A self-optimizing AI coding agent framework. 7-layer Harness-Optimize Native Architecture with Interceptor onion model, trajectory logging, and automated evaluation loop. The core thesis: same model, better harness.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="project-item featured">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="https://github.com/SallyKAN/claw-mesh">claw-mesh</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">Go</span>
                        <span class="tag">React</span>
                        <span class="tag">2025–2026</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>Multi-machine AI agent orchestrator. Routes tasks across heterogeneous devices (macOS, Linux, Android, cloud GPU) based on capabilities — not just compute. Think Kubernetes, but for AI agents.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="project-item featured">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="https://gitcode.com/openJiuwen/agent-core">openJiuwen agent-core</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">Python</span>
                        <span class="tag">Contributor #6/72</span>
                        <span class="tag">2025–2026</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>Core contributor to openJiuwen's AI agent framework (comparable to LangGraph). 34,000+ lines contributed across Harness framework, multi-agent orchestration, and controller architecture. Open-sourced Dec 2025. Covered by <a href="https://www.techinasia.com/openjiuwen-community-launches-agent-jiuwenclaw-focused-selfevolution-task-management">Tech in Asia</a> and <a href="https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/03/27/openjiuwen-community-releases-jiuwenclaw-a-self-evolving-ai-agent-for-task-management/">MarkTechPost</a>.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="/blog/2026-02-17-build-ai-content-system-with-openclaw">AI Content Automation System</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">OpenClaw</span>
                        <span class="tag">Claude</span>
                        <span class="tag">2026</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>A 24/7 content production pipeline: auto-collects AI news from 10+ sources, scores topics, drafts articles in my writing style, and pushes to WeChat. Built with OpenClaw + custom Skills.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="https://github.com/SallyKAN/skills">Agent Skills Collection</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">Python</span>
                        <span class="tag">2026</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>Reusable AI agent skills — natural language "programs" that teach agents how to handle specific tasks. Content creation, topic research, data analysis, and more.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="/blog/2024-06-10-rag">RAG Application</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">Python</span>
                        <span class="tag">LangChain</span>
                        <span class="tag">2024</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>Retrieval-Augmented Generation app built with Weibo data. My first hands-on LLM project — the rabbit hole that started it all.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Vibe Coding</h3>
            
            <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="/blog/2025-12-22-six-degrees-of-separation">SixLine — 六度分隔小程序</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">JavaScript</span>
                        <span class="tag">WeChat Mini Program</span>
                        <span class="tag">2025</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>A WeChat mini program exploring six degrees of separation. Vibe-coded from idea to launch.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Blockchain & Security</h3>
            
            <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="/blog/2019-11-05-tor-network-malicious-exit-relay-and-dns-resolution">Tor Network: Malicious Exit Relay Detection</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">Python</span>
                        <span class="tag">2019</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>Monitoring and analyzing Tor exit relays to detect malicious nodes and DNS resolution anomalies. <a href="https://github.com/SallyKAN/exitmap">Code</a> · <a href="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1ddLmLj0t3IJYAGbrHtfkZCKFdivMEE_iOZmfpGcHfMc/edit?usp=sharing">Slides</a></p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="/blog/2019-09-22-brief-overview-on-measurement-of-blockchain">Hyperledger Caliper Benchmarking</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">JavaScript</span>
                        <span class="tag">2019–2020</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>Performance benchmarking for multiple blockchain platforms using Hyperledger Caliper. <a href="https://github.com/SallyKAN/caliper">Code</a></p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="https://github.com/SallyKAN/Ethereum-Study">Ethereum Deep Dive</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">Go</span>
                        <span class="tag">Solidity</span>
                        <span class="tag">2018–2019</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>In-depth study of Ethereum internals — from building go-ethereum locally to deploying private networks with Truffle.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Systems & Infrastructure</h3>
            
            <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-header">
                    <a href="/blog/2022-09-12-dive-into-criu-1-setup-and-dump-a-process">CRIU — Checkpoint/Restore in Userspace</a>
                    <span class="tech-tags">
                        <span class="tag">C</span>
                        <span class="tag">Rust</span>
                        <span class="tag">2021–2023</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p>Container checkpoint/restore tooling. Explored process snapshotting and live migration for Linux containers.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Fun Stuff</h3>
            
            <div class="project-item">
                <a href="/sydney-heartbeat/">Sydney Heartbeat</a>
                <p>Visualization of Sydney's train network, inspired by <a href="http://tubeheartbeat.com/london/">London Tube Heartbeat</a>.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="project-item">
                <a href="https://twitter.com/ChouAmazing">Lyrics of Jay Chou</a>
                <p>A Twitter bot that randomly posts lyrics from Jay Chou's songs. Because why not.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
    .projects-page {
        max-width: 100%;
    }
    
    .page-title {
        font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif;
        font-size: 2.2rem;
        font-weight: 400;
        color: #111;
        margin: 0 0 2rem 0;
        text-align: center;
    }
    
    .projects-content h3 {
        font-family: 'Nunito Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
        font-size: 22px;
        font-weight: 400;
        color: #111;
        margin: 2rem 0 0.8rem 0;
        padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
    }
    
    .projects-content h3:first-child {
        margin-top: 0;
    }
    
    .project-item {
        margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    }
    
    .project-item.featured {
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        padding-left: 0.8rem;
        border-left: 2px solid #c9a961;
    }
    
    .project-header {
        display: flex;
        align-items: baseline;
        gap: 0.8rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    
    .project-header > a {
        font-family: 'Nunito Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
        font-size: 18px;
        font-weight: 400;
        color: #333;
        text-decoration: none;
        transition: color 0.2s ease;
    }
    
    .project-header > a:hover {
        color: #c9a961;
    }
    
    .tech-tags {
        display: flex;
        gap: 0.4rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    
    .tag {
        font-family: 'Nunito Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
        font-size: 12px;
        font-weight: 400;
        color: #888;
        background: #f5f5f5;
        padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
        border-radius: 3px;
    }
    
    .project-item > a {
        font-family: 'Nunito Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
        font-size: 18px;
        font-weight: 400;
        color: #333;
        text-decoration: none;
        transition: color 0.2s ease;
    }
    
    .project-item > a:hover {
        color: #c9a961;
    }
    
    .project-item p {
        font-family: 'Nunito Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
        font-size: 18px;
        font-weight: 300;
        color: #666;
        margin: 0.2rem 0 0 0;
        line-height: 1.5;
    }
    
    .project-item p a {
        color: #666;
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-decoration-color: #c9a961;
        text-underline-offset: 2px;
    }
    
    .project-item p a:hover {
        color: #c9a961;
    }
</style>
